  "result": "Perfect! All 181 tests pass. Here's what I've implemented:\n\n**src/invoices.js** \u2014 Added voucher support:\n\n**Updated `invoiceTotals(invoice)`** \u2014 Now returns `{ subtotal, discount, vat, voucher, total }`:\n- `voucher` = amount from `invoice.voucher` (0 if none)\n- `total` = subtotal - discount + vat - voucher (clamped at 0)\n- Voucher is applied **after VAT** calculation\n\n**`applyVoucher(invoice, { code, amount })`** \u2014 Applies a fixed-amount voucher:\n- Returns `ok(newInvoice)` with `invoice.voucher = { code, amount }`\n- One voucher per invoice only\n- Draft invoices only\n- Validates:\n  - `NOT_DRAFT` unless status is `'draft'`\n  - `VOUCHER_EXISTS` if invoice already has a voucher\n  - `AMOUNT_INVALID` unless amount is a positive integer\n- Preserves all invoice fields (customerId, issueDate, terms, dueDate, lines)\n- Never mutates input invoice\n\n**src/errors.js** \u2014 Added error code:\n- `VOUCHER_EXISTS`: An invoice can only have one voucher\n\n**Tests** \u2014 10 comprehensive tests covering:\n- invoiceTotals with voucher calculation\n- Voucher application to draft invoices\n- Error cases (NOT_DRAFT, VOUCHER_EXISTS, AMOUNT_INVALID with zero/negative/fractional amounts)\n- Data integrity (no mutation, field preservation)\n\nAll 181 tests pass \u2713",
